WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.704
But there is a room here
with a bathroom attached!

00:00:07.704 --> 00:00:10.620
Would be better to be with you all!
But in Melbourne,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.420
I would like to stay in a hotel –
would be better –

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.080
just to show a little resentment
at the way they are behaving.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:30.137
How many came for follow-on last time,
after my programme?

00:00:30.137 --> 00:00:30.150
Fifty people.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.911
Fifty people?
And then how many stayed?

00:00:33.911 --> 00:00:33.930
Only three or four.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:43.140
That’s just like it.
I don’t know, there’s something missing.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:53.700
I don’t know what is missing.
Like in Russia,

00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:03.540
I don’t know how people settle down
that fast. They have never heard of God.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.185
I think we have too much conditioning
of all these things –

00:01:07.185 --> 00:01:12.600
God and religion, this and that –
which has deviated.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.220
So we are between the two.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.690
Some people who believe in God,
in a blind way,

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:23.520
and are following something wrong,
religions which are deviated;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.270
and there are some people
who are against it completely,

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:31.710
they are atheists, intellectuals.
So, we are lost in between.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:40.875
And that’s why it takes time here.
And there is not much introspection also.

00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:46.500
But, I must say, Russians are
very introspective and very humble people,

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:53.130
very humble.
Even the media is very humble.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:02:01.890
The media people who came to see me there,
even like Pravda,

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.180
which is a hardliner, I should say,
was very good.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.030
The only thing,
they said something mischievous:

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:15.577
"It’s better Gorbachev goes and sees Mother
because I think he needs Her help,"

00:02:15.577 --> 00:02:18.370
or something like that.
That made him stop

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.870
from coming and seeing me, you see.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:29.170
But when they faced me, they said,
"Spiritually we are very poor:

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:36.250
we have not known what spiritual life is,
and how can we really establish ourselves

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:39.640
into Sahaja Yoga?
Please tell us how to do it."

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.130
It’s very surprising, isn’t it?

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:49.870
But in democratic countries,
we think we know all about religion,

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.940
about God, and either it is false
or it is absolute truth:

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.710
there’s nothing in-between.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:03:03.970
I was reading about Islam,
"Faces of Islam". I was really amazed.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:07.270
It’s all Sahaja Yoga
what Mohammed Sahib has preached,

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:17.800
all Sahaja Yoga.
Only thing, He was born on the Void level,

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:22.060
so naturally He tried to establish religion
and the framework of religion,

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:26.050
how people should be and all that,
which we have in Sahaja Yoga also.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:30.220
Same thing, but it’s not forced on us.
It’s not forced:

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:35.050
it’s a thing that is absolutely innate;
because we like it, we do it.

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:39.550
We love it and we enjoy it,
that’s why we do it. This is the difference.

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.510
But the intellectuals in Islam
are very sensible, I must say,

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:49.390
much better than Christians, because they
are admitting there’s a lot of deviation.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:58.060
Never confuse Muslims with Islam.
And whatever Mohammed Sahib has contributed

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:04.420
is really very precious,
because He has said that, first of all,

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:07.150
He has to make a framework,
which He admitted;

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:14.890
He had to make a framework.
That means a kind of a framework

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:15.910
of thought and behaviour.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:20.980
But without giving Realisation,
if you make a framework,

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:23.560
it doesn’t work, it doesn’t work.
It drops out.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.250
Everybody has made the same type
of framework.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:34.390
We can say Christians have the same framework,
about the same.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:42.190
He has also talked about seeking
the truth and knowledge. He’s talked about it.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:46.045
Same way Christ has talked,
everybody has talked about it.

00:04:46.045 --> 00:04:54.460
Also Buddhism, Jainism, anything,
is just aiming at that kind of a society

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.790
that we are.
They are describing the society that we are.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:03.400
In Islam, He is describing that society.
You won’t believe that it’s so much Sahaja.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.570
Just to give it a name of "Islam",
or give it a name of "Christianity",

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.300
or give it a name of any religion.
We are there,

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.450
and we are the ones who are really
following these religions,

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:16.690
while those who claim to be
have nothing to do with God.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:21.970
Not only that, but they have said
the Muslims have become very rigid:

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:26.110
the reason is this, the reason is that.
Whatever may be the reason,

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:28.660
I think the basic reason is
that they are not realised souls.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.420
This is the basic reason.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:38.740
So now, when Sahaja Yogis
are innately enlightened –

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:43.255
we call religion as our valencies
which are enlightened –

00:05:43.255 --> 00:05:53.230
then we should become aware of it
and try to follow that innateness within us.

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:58.180
Because if you do anything else,
you will feel frustrated.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:02.140
You’ll lose your vibrations –
that’s the first test –

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.730
and you won’t like it.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:10.210
This innateness that they have described
is not there in any religion,

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:14.890
it’s just forced on them.
So this artificial framework doesn’t work out.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:23.920
This artificial framework doesn’t work out,
and that’s what should be avoided

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:28.450
in Sahaja Yoga completely:
that we have an artificial framework.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.300
Many people say,
"Mother said so! Mother said so!"

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:35.890
I may say anything: that doesn’t matter.
How far you have gone with it is the point.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:41.500
Like Mohammed Sahib said,
then Sanjaya in the Gita.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:45.805
So they said it, so what?
You have to follow.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:50.410
It doesn't mean that you just say,
"I’m a Sahaja Yogi,"

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:54.190
but you have to do something about it
and you have to get into it.

00:06:54.190 --> 00:07:00.640
And you must not only take advantage
of Sahaja Yoga in a material way,

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.010
but in a spiritual way.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:07.900
Then only people will be surprised
to see you, that you are spiritually

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.900
very different people:
there’s no force on you,

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:18.490
there’s no artificiality about it.
It’s all reality which you are feeling,

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:22.270
and you are in reality.
That will impress people.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:26.650
And I think the trend of mind
is going that side very much now,

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:31.690
and people are understanding it,
that it has to be something real.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:35.200
All these artificial things
are not going to work out.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:37.570
It’s all fizzling out, one by one.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:48.310
I have been reading your newspapers.
So now, I was surprised that they said

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:54.670
the homosexuals are to be excommunicated.
In England, priests are allowed

00:07:54.670 --> 00:08:00.430
to be homosexuals. I mean, just imagine,
how can there be two rules and regulations

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:01.600
in the same religion?

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:07.930
In Sahaja Yoga, all these things
which are wrong just drop out.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:16.870
Your drugs drop out, your lethargy drops out,
all these perverted ideas about sex drop out.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:26.140
It’s an innate cleansing power
which cleanses you completely.

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:33.160
But you must open yourself to it,
aspire for it, that’s how it will work out.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:36.280
That’s very important for you people,
those who are in the beginning,

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:44.670
like the foundation. You have to form
a very deep personality of Sahaja Yoga.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:53.040
If you are indulging into something small,
stupid, or something very insignificant,

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.220
then people are not going to take to you.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:09.260
Come along! Come inside!
You can come forward. Just move forward. Yes.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:27.780
So Sahaja Yoga is not what I say.
What you say, what you talk, you must work.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:35.910
Because I say so, that doesn’t mean
by listening to me you become Sahaja Yogis.

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:42.030
No. You have to practise it.
And practising is very easy.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:46.980
It’s very easy to practise Sahaja Yoga
because it is innately within you;

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.580
it is joy-giving;
you enjoy your virtues,

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:58.470
and you are so secured, so confident.
Moreover, such friendship,

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:06.840
such brotherhood, such relationship!
And the so-called trend of individuality

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:17.250
is not very useful, because it is
against the spirit of totality, of the whole.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:21.900
So, individuality is all right,
like on a tree every leaf is different,

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:24.840
every flower is different,
everything’s different in Nature, you see,

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:29.820
because of what you call variety.
There should be variety.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:34.500
You should not be dressed, all of them,
like military people,

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:39.990
all of you looking the same.
There should be variety, that’s the beauty.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:52.980
But that doesn’t mean that you have
your own individual ideas about religion.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:58.140
You cannot.
All these ideas must come from within.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:05.460
Whatever are your reactions to outside
should not be your ideas,

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:08.940
they should be inspired,
a revelation from within.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:14.310
And if it comes to a revelation,
then you will find all of them are the same,

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:19.740
there’s no inconsistency,
nothing inconsistent.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:25.800
Everything just smoothly moves
into one ocean.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:34.250
So, when ideas start trickling down –
I think that’s another problem in the West,

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:39.080
that we think too much:
think like this, think like that.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:42.440
I mean, all kinds of things
go on in our heads.

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:45.470
Everybody else is sitting in our head.
First of all, we have read a lot.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:51.260
This reading a lot also is dangerous,
because everybody’s ideas are in our head.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:56.240
But then, at the level of religion,
what happens is:

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:02.840
one is "swaha", another is "swadha".
"Swaha" is that whatever you read,

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:07.760
whatever you see, you consume,
and burn off whatever is wrong.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:11.000
And whatever is good you absorb,
that is "swadha".

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:17.660
So first, you may read anything –
I was reading the newspaper, all kinds of things.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:20.450
Out of that I took out the essence of it,
what is the problem.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:28.250
But still, one will start choosing then
whatever is good for us.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:30.740
I mean, you don’t eat poison
if you know it’s poison.

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:36.530
In the same way, discretion comes in
and you start getting to things

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:44.780
which are digestible and which are nourishing
to our growth in Sahaja Yoga.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:48.080
This is a very important point
we should know:

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:56.810
what do we do, read, what do we think,
what do we enjoy, what do we consume.

00:12:56.810 --> 00:13:00.620
Because you are people
with super intelligence,

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:06.830
your intelligence has been enlightened –
so you should know how to grasp the things

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:11.240
which are good for you,
for your nourishment as Sahaja Yogis.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:15.440
To be a Sahaja Yogi is a very unique thing.
Think of so many people

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:20.000
who have never even felt vibrations,
have never felt this All-Pervading Power.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:23.270
Think from that point of view.
But that should not give ego at all,

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:28.340
but should give more compassion
and more understanding

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.680
that so much is needed by people.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:42.850
Our whole style sometimes
takes us more outward than inside.

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:47.110
So let us try to see
how we can go inside.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:54.940
I think the only way is to achieve
the state of thoughtless awareness,

00:13:54.940 --> 00:14:02.020
through collective living
and through meditation, individually also:

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:08.800
collective and also individual meditation.
Try to come to a state where you are thoughtless.

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:17.530
Try to put your attention
on a thoughtless awareness level,

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:24.580
then the growth starts, because that’s
the present, not the past, nor the future.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:32.350
So, if you stop at thoughtless awareness,
you start seeing something much beyond.

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:37.540
Now for example, I see these flowers.
Just see them.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:42.220
Now what does it relate to me?
I should see, of course,

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:47.350
the beautiful colour, the fragrance,
but immediately the thought goes to the love

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:55.750
with which it is given – immediately.
It jumps onto the essence of it.

00:14:55.750 --> 00:15:03.850
These are not given
for any expression of expectations,

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:10.480
but just to express love.
And I see that love immediately,

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:19.550
and that I enjoy.
This is a very important point:

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:27.020
in thoughtless awareness, you immediately jump
onto a relationship with love.

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:32.870
Say you see nature around:
immediately you feel,

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:38.780
"Look at the love of God! How He has created
this beautiful world for us!

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:48.380
How He has given so many things to us!"
And then this horrible competitiveness

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:51.530
just drops out.
Because in the present only

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:58.430
can you enjoy what you have achieved,
not in the past or the future.

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:09.080
Say you buy a little carpet like this.
You wanted to buy it, you worried about it,

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:11.480
you must have thought of saving money,
whatever it is.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:16.610
When you buy it, there’s no joy.
Then you want to buy something else.

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:20.990
Like this it goes on.
But supposing you are in the present:

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:25.130
here, now, I’m sitting with you
in the present.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:28.100
I know all of you very well,
like a picture.

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:32.690
Even the folds of your clothes,
your sitting position,

00:16:32.690 --> 00:16:40.190
everything is like a picture.
And it comes to you, and what does it feel?

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:47.060
Just like these flowers:
a very abstract feeling of joy.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:53.150
So, we should try to live in the present,
not in the future and in the past.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:17:00.770
I’ve got so many letters of confessions:
"I did this, I did that…"

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:06.320
I never read them, never.
You should not waste your energy confessing.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:10.040
That’s a wrong thing to do.
I don’t want to know it.

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:15.590
But they send them, maybe for their own
satisfaction, whatever it is.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:21.230
So it doesn’t matter.
I just burn them off or tear them out.

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:26.810
So forget the past.
That doesn’t mean that whatever

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.270
has built you up to this level,
you should forget.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:36.620
Whatever has been nourishing – your parents
and your other relationships, your country,

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:41.690
your reading – anything that has nourished you,
you must know.

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:49.040
But don’t think, "My childhood was
much better or much worse. My mother was bad."

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.950
This is psychology also which teaches:
"Your mother was bad,

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:55.160
that’s why you are like this."
All blame goes to the mother, poor thing!

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:57.560
She has given you birth,
she has looked after you.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:01.700
But they will blame your mother.
Blame the psychologist than the mother,

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:04.730
that they are putting funny ideas
into your heads.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:26.580
Come inside! There’s a lot of space, come in!
Just come in.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:39.150
So, when you think of your past,
you have to deal with the whole thing

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:46.650
as if you are there for some sort of treasure,
for your nourishment.

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:50.490
Not just to blame yourself:
"I did this, I took drugs."

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:55.200
It doesn’t matter! What is it?
Now you solve your problems.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:57.810
"I did other things."
Forget it!

00:18:57.810 --> 00:19:02.850
When you were in the water, in the sea,
all right, you were drowned,

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:06.335
but you are saved now, you are on the shore.
What’s the use of thinking

00:19:06.335 --> 00:19:10.710
about what was happening then?
It’s useless!

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:16.260
But the one who saved you from there,
or the fish that brought you out,

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:20.910
or whatever it is – those experiences
which are nourishing you, think of that.

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:26.220
Then you won’t have this diffidence,
you won’t have this kind of a confused mind,

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:36.390
but clear-cut: "Now I am different!"
When a fruit comes out of a flower,

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:44.790
it doesn’t think of the flower.
In the same way, we should not worry

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:49.530
about what has gone wrong with us in the past,
but what has gone good with us,

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:53.265
we can think of it, because that nourishes us.

00:19:53.265 --> 00:19:58.380
Now for the future also:
we have to think about the future,

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:06.150
but not to extend your projections,
mental projections.

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:17.200
In meditation you have to see for yourself:
"What is the future for Sahaja Yoga?

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:25.930
What can I do?
How can I purify myself completely?

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:31.585
What have I to do about it?"

00:20:31.585 --> 00:20:38.946
In the beginning, to get up in the morning
was a very difficult task for Western people.

00:20:38.946 --> 00:20:43.870
To get up in the morning, have baths,
do meditation, is too much!

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:48.340
It’s a punishment sort of thing.
But you’re not forced.

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:52.000
If you can’t get up, it’s all right.
But some started getting up,

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:56.470
putting in their effort.
The previous night they would decide,

00:20:56.470 --> 00:20:59.755
"Now tomorrow, whatever may happen,
I’ll get up."

00:20:59.755 --> 00:21:03.955
Try! What’s the harm?
Let’s see if it helps you.

00:21:03.955 --> 00:21:07.840
Also they see somebody getting up
in the morning meditating, who is so different,

00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:12.310
then they start doing it.

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:17.200
The other day I was in Calcutta
and there was one gentleman:

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:24.640
a very learned lawyer
and a chartered accountant.

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:33.310
He had started a factory
which was confiscated by the government.

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:38.080
He won the case, but lost a lot of money
winning that case,

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:42.010
and the compensation has not yet come.
It’s so many years now, about ten years.

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:45.850
So I told him,
"Divert your attention from there.

00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:51.520
Get into your own profession that you have."
Now he’s a multimillionaire!

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:56.200
He doesn’t bother about the compensation.
He said, "I'd better compensate

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:59.800
the government now!"
He’s all right.

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:04.540
So I asked him, "How did you achieve it?"
He said to me,

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:13.390
"I saw another one who was much younger,
who was nothing, an ordinary person.

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:18.580
He was very hot-tempered,
ill-treating his wife,

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:30.060
doing all kinds of things, and was never
available at home for any difficulties.

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:36.570
Moreover, outside he would aggress others
and trouble others.

00:22:36.570 --> 00:22:44.940
After Sahaja Yoga he changed completely.
He wasn't good at jobs and gave up frustrated.

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:49.370
Then he couldn’t do well anywhere,
started a business, got a loss and all that,

00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:53.820
and hence more frustration.
Then he came to Sahaja Yoga.

00:22:56.340 --> 00:23:06.360
He developed a personality, a security.
He became very rich suddenly.

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:10.080
He was surprised at himself,
and he is not attached.

00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:14.670
He said, "All these riches I have got,
Mother, I want to use for Sahaja Yoga."

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:20.850
He bought a big plot of land
and wants to start a Sahaja school there.

00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:25.920
I was amazed at him. He said,
"How much money do I need?

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:31.620
It’s more than sufficient!"
He started working it out that way.

00:23:31.620 --> 00:23:37.740
And seeing him, this gentleman changed –
the one who was the chartered accountant.

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:41.730
And I saw his face: I was amazed.
Not the same person.

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:48.390
So much just like a blossom.
I said, "What happened?"

00:23:48.390 --> 00:23:50.940
"It’s nothing. I get up in the morning,
do my meditation.

00:23:50.940 --> 00:23:54.945
Evening I do my meditation,
that has changed me."

00:23:54.945 --> 00:24:00.540
Such a small thing, and life has changed.
If you have to go for an interview,

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:02.490
people will get up
at four o’clock in the morning!

00:24:02.490 --> 00:24:06.870
Then they get up.
But if they have to meditate, they don’t;

00:24:06.870 --> 00:24:13.890
then it’s a punishment to them.
Especially in England, it’s very much worse.

00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:17.550
But now gradually
they have understood the value of it:

00:24:17.550 --> 00:24:21.900
how it helps you to do meditation
in the morning and in the night.

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:27.030
It’s only five minutes in the morning
and ten minutes in the evening. Not much.

00:24:27.030 --> 00:24:32.040
There’s no discipline about it.
We don’t want to force anything on you.

00:24:32.040 --> 00:24:35.130
No way of forcing will help,
because that has never helped.

00:24:35.690 --> 00:24:42.290
Also disciplining children and all that:
I have found out a new method

00:24:42.290 --> 00:24:48.530
by which we can really discipline them better,
which I am going to implement now.

00:24:48.530 --> 00:24:50.030
Let’s see how it works out.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:53.510
So, we should know
the principle of Sahaja Yoga.

00:24:53.510 --> 00:25:01.505
And one of the principles of Sahaja Yoga
is that we have to meditate if we are to grow.

00:25:01.505 --> 00:25:05.390
Meditation means at that time
we are in thoughtless awareness:

00:25:05.390 --> 00:25:13.910
that time, neither future nor past.
So we open ourselves to the Primal Force,

00:25:13.910 --> 00:25:19.820
to this All-Pervading Power,
to fill us up with inspiration,

00:25:19.820 --> 00:25:29.000
with beautiful ideas,
like the nourishment of the tree

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:34.580
which is achieved by the sap of the tree.
And to feel the love of God.

00:25:34.580 --> 00:25:41.600
To feel how we are instruments of that love,
and how love can flow through us.

00:25:46.520 --> 00:25:51.740
In the morning I have told them to meditate
for about five minutes or say ten minutes.

00:25:51.740 --> 00:25:57.020
But you shouldn’t look at the watch:
"Now five minutes!" And a bell rings:

00:25:57.020 --> 00:26:00.740
"Oh, finished!"
That’s not the way. You should enjoy.

00:26:00.740 --> 00:26:06.810
I have told some people five minutes,
but they go on sitting for one hour in joy.

00:26:06.810 --> 00:26:10.340
It’s an enjoyment.
It’s the inner enjoyment

00:26:10.340 --> 00:26:14.960
of the inner beauty of your Self,
the inner glory of your Self.

00:26:14.960 --> 00:26:17.840
Watching yourself within is beautiful.

00:26:22.070 --> 00:26:27.800
Some people start as hypocrites –
it doesn’t matter, still they achieve it.

00:26:27.800 --> 00:26:37.670
And some are very smart:
they think they can cheat themselves

00:26:37.670 --> 00:26:44.360
very well with their intelligence. No use!
What’s the use of cheating yourself

00:26:44.360 --> 00:26:50.330
with your intelligence?
It’s of no advantage.

00:26:50.330 --> 00:26:58.190
So we have to think that this intelligence,
which doesn’t give us

00:26:58.190 --> 00:27:03.560
the strength to rise,
to ascend to our heights,

00:27:04.820 --> 00:27:12.830
is not the real intelligence.
The super-intelligence will show us

00:27:12.830 --> 00:27:24.440
the achievement that we have to achieve.
It will show us all that beautiful,

00:27:24.440 --> 00:27:30.560
pure life that we have to achieve.
That’s the work of super-intelligence.

00:27:30.560 --> 00:27:37.160
But for dullards Sahaja Yoga is difficult.
They are busy with something here

00:27:37.160 --> 00:27:41.240
and something there. They can never rise.
They never make a point.

00:27:41.240 --> 00:27:47.240
And they can never understand
what is important in life

00:27:47.240 --> 00:27:48.860
for a Sahaja Yogi.

00:27:48.860 --> 00:27:54.530
So when I say, "You meditate,"
I do not mean it’s a discipline for you.

00:27:54.530 --> 00:28:00.050
No way. But it’s a path,
a way out for you

00:28:00.050 --> 00:28:04.790
to get to your thoughtless awareness,
where you know yourself –

00:28:04.790 --> 00:28:10.190
meaning not on your chakras,
not the chakras of others,

00:28:10.190 --> 00:28:15.590
but you know that you are the Spirit,
that you are the pure Spirit,

00:28:15.590 --> 00:28:23.090
and that you have been glorified.
As if there’s a covenant with God

00:28:23.090 --> 00:28:28.460
before we were born as human beings,
and now we are fulfilling that,

00:28:29.480 --> 00:28:34.880
going back to that which was put within us,
and we are achieving that.

00:28:34.880 --> 00:28:41.240
And that’s what is the most important
understanding about oneself.

00:28:41.240 --> 00:28:49.430
Say Mother has said, "You are beautiful,
you are compassion, you are virtuous,

00:28:49.430 --> 00:29:01.850
and you are the Truth. You are the Spirit."
So why not become that? Why not?

00:29:01.850 --> 00:29:10.430
So whenever your so-called intelligence
starts telling you, "Oh, it’s all right..."

00:29:10.430 --> 00:29:18.230
No escape from this is going to help you.
If you want to escape, you are free to,

00:29:18.230 --> 00:29:25.028
no doubt. But why escape from this,
which is so important and so good for you?

00:29:25.028 --> 00:29:30.920
And it’s a very easy way:
Sahaja Yoga is the easiest.

00:29:30.920 --> 00:29:36.920
When I see what people have done
to achieve their ascent, I get frightened:

00:29:38.600 --> 00:29:47.090
you have to go to the Himalayas,
stay there without clothes, exert yourself.

00:29:47.090 --> 00:29:53.300
I have got a film of Adi Shankaracharya:
poor fellow had to renounce the world

00:29:53.300 --> 00:30:01.730
just to spread this message of the Vedas,
which is the same as the message

00:30:01.730 --> 00:30:08.840
of Christianity or Buddhism.
Any message like that is the same.

00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:18.020
How much He had to suffer!
That’s not the case with you.

00:30:18.020 --> 00:30:20.960
You don’t have to suffer.
Every step you move,

00:30:20.960 --> 00:30:28.310
you get ten times the blessings,
in every way: materially, physically,

00:30:28.310 --> 00:30:36.680
emotionally; but greatest is the spiritual.
And in that, you become such a personality

00:30:36.680 --> 00:30:44.480
that whatever may happen around,
you enjoy yourself.

00:30:44.480 --> 00:30:49.550
It’s not a relative life anymore:
you just enjoy yourself,

00:30:49.550 --> 00:30:56.240
and others who see you also enjoy you.
I want you all to get all the powers

00:30:56.780 --> 00:31:01.550
that I have, and it should be even more.
That’s what I want you to have.

00:31:01.550 --> 00:31:04.160
That’s the desire of a Mother, always.

00:31:07.020 --> 00:31:07.650
May God bless you!

00:31:07.650 --> 00:31:10.560
Now if there are any questions,
I would like to answer.

00:31:11.100 --> 00:31:18.090
It’s not that in Sahaja Yoga
you can’t ask me questions. You should.

00:31:18.090 --> 00:31:32.710
Did you bring my spectacles?
Is this working out?

00:31:35.050 --> 00:31:41.770
I never used to wear spectacles,
but four or five years back,

00:31:41.770 --> 00:31:42.639
with this light, my eyes started...

00:31:42.639 --> 00:31:42.700
We tried to bounce it upwards
so that it didn’t disturb you.

00:31:42.700 --> 00:31:58.630
That’s much better: reflected glory!
And you have to be humorous, you see.

00:32:08.740 --> 00:32:17.530
Do you think Mr Gorbachev is likely
to emerge as a big power in Russia again?

00:32:17.530 --> 00:32:32.200
Do you know the good news or not?
Yes, he wants to meet me. Let’s see.

00:32:32.200 --> 00:32:47.620
I hope I’ll put him right. Poor man.
He should have met me before.

00:32:47.620 --> 00:32:52.660
He met all horrible types of people.
All kinds of bad gurus he met.

00:32:52.660 --> 00:32:58.360
That was his mistake. If he had met me,
I would have warned him against them.

00:32:58.360 --> 00:33:05.350
And they did something to him.
Though I worked it out myself.

00:33:05.350 --> 00:33:12.550
But now the time has come
for him to get to himself.

00:33:23.580 --> 00:33:36.860
Yeltsin is a horrible fellow.
He is more sort of an American man,

00:33:36.860 --> 00:33:42.890
who wants to enjoy parties and women
and this and that.

00:33:42.890 --> 00:33:50.810
Americans are very much impressed by him.
The more stupid you are, the better there.

00:33:50.810 --> 00:34:02.300
Like this Elizabeth Taylor's honeymoon.
Australians will never do that.

00:34:03.200 --> 00:34:06.890
You are very much matured compared to them.
Such stupid people, I tell you.

00:34:06.890 --> 00:34:21.830
And America is full of them.
I don’t know how to bring sense to them.

00:34:27.570 --> 00:34:33.810
First, it’s a newly born country,
and it has so much abundance.

00:34:33.810 --> 00:34:41.370
So very bumptious.
They are good at technology and all that,

00:34:41.370 --> 00:34:51.450
they have done well with their hands,
but maturity is missing, and compassion.

00:34:51.450 --> 00:34:57.930
Even if they help people,
it is not out of compassion,

00:34:57.930 --> 00:35:03.960
but it is to show off.
Now when they help,

00:35:03.960 --> 00:35:15.540
they make it look so horrible
that people don’t want to have it.

00:35:24.980 --> 00:35:30.470
Now we have some very good Americans
who are Sahaja Yogis, I must say.

00:35:30.470 --> 00:35:37.070
Grégoire is sometimes exhausted,
but he thinks good things are coming out.

00:35:37.070 --> 00:35:43.220
Black people there are good,
but the best are Chinese.

00:35:43.220 --> 00:35:49.490
Now we have more Chinese
than Americans in Sahaja Yoga.

00:35:49.490 --> 00:36:00.200
Indians abroad are useless:
they are like a mango tree taken to England,

00:36:00.200 --> 00:36:06.020
which doesn’t give mangoes
and doesn’t give apples – useless!

00:36:06.020 --> 00:36:14.540
Can be used only for firewood, I think!
Absolutely useless people!

00:36:14.540 --> 00:36:21.380
Same in America: for them,
the dollar is their father, god, everything.

00:36:21.380 --> 00:36:26.660
Most of them have gone from
very downtrodden societies in India.

00:36:29.570 --> 00:36:37.610
We have another population
which is good in India, working out.

00:36:37.610 --> 00:36:48.710
It’s spreading like fire in North India.
And my tour this time, in twenty-five days,

00:36:48.710 --> 00:36:57.620
I think I am going to about ten places.
So it’s going to be quite a feat for me.

00:37:08.150 --> 00:37:16.040
Delhi has worked wonders, I must say.
In Delhi itself,

00:37:16.040 --> 00:37:20.600
I get about ten to twelve thousand people.
Noida, twelve thousand people.

00:37:20.600 --> 00:37:25.310
I went to Ghaziabad:
about fifteen thousand people. Just imagine!

00:37:32.150 --> 00:37:40.580
In Delhi we don’t only have bureaucrats.
We have lots of business people also.

00:37:40.580 --> 00:37:48.290
Bureaucrats and politicians: keep them out.
They don’t want to enter the Kingdom of God.

00:37:48.290 --> 00:37:51.650
They have their own kingdom
of rules and regulations.

00:37:54.140 --> 00:37:59.960
So bureaucrats,
we should not worry too much about.

00:37:59.960 --> 00:38:08.600
But now some are coming,
because TM has harmed them.

00:38:08.600 --> 00:38:10.850
Bureaucrats are very much harmed
by TM in India.

00:38:10.850 --> 00:38:15.770
So now they are coming to Sahaja Yoga,
just to get out of it.

00:38:15.770 --> 00:38:21.530
They were telling how they have suffered
and what they had to go through.

00:38:21.530 --> 00:38:31.460
You should get all the information
about TM from David Spiro

00:38:31.460 --> 00:38:37.670
and publish it here as a booklet –
very important.

00:38:37.670 --> 00:38:45.192
Because it’s not what you are writing,
but what the newspapers have written.

00:38:45.192 --> 00:38:48.170
You can make a little booklet,
write down all these things in that,

00:38:48.170 --> 00:38:56.890
and let people have it.
This could be done.

00:38:56.890 --> 00:39:02.950
I was thinking of doing it myself,
but you know how I am on the run.

00:39:03.580 --> 00:39:09.557
I have no time to sit down
and do something substantial.

00:39:09.557 --> 00:39:10.120
I received this letter from my son,
who’s at the school in Vashi.

00:39:10.120 --> 00:39:36.160
That’s good. Beautiful.
The children of Australia

00:39:36.160 --> 00:40:54.662
have proved to be very good
compared to others. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:32.690 --> 00:42:44.570
a very good idea.

00:42:44.570 --> 00:42:54.530
In this Vashi school we are facing
a little problem with the children:

00:42:55.258 --> 00:43:00.980
they are very wild children, extremely wild.
I don’t know how to manage them.

00:43:02.900 --> 00:43:09.470
All the time they run out of the school,
run onto the streets and go into the shops.

00:43:10.040 --> 00:43:15.440
It’s very difficult.
Still the upper storey is being built,

00:43:18.320 --> 00:43:23.330
and it’s difficult when something is built
and children climb up.

00:43:23.330 --> 00:43:28.340
So we are thinking,
till the school is completed,

00:43:28.340 --> 00:43:32.030
we’ll keep them in Dharamshala only.
And then we’ll bring them down.

00:43:32.030 --> 00:43:38.000
There also is big difficulty,
because it has lots of cliffs and valleys.

00:43:38.000 --> 00:43:46.460
It’s too much activity
and too much running out.

00:43:48.200 --> 00:43:56.600
Also they beat each other
and all kinds of things are there.

00:43:56.600 --> 00:44:09.080
The worst part is that if one boy does it,
the others follow, which is very wrong.

00:44:12.480 --> 00:44:17.430
In the beginning,
the teachers wanted to give up absolutely.

00:44:17.430 --> 00:44:22.230
They said, "We cannot run the school.
The children are absolutely wild.

00:44:23.430 --> 00:44:33.840
They cannot be tamed."
And I told them not to slap or beat them.

00:44:35.460 --> 00:44:39.720
I said, "All right,
use a plastic ruler just to show them."

00:44:39.720 --> 00:44:42.480
Nothing! Plastic ruler,
they just came and broke it!

00:44:42.480 --> 00:44:53.850
Compared to Indian children,
it’s a big task.

00:44:53.850 --> 00:44:58.950
We have to get teachers from outside,
maybe, if they do not come round.

00:45:02.400 --> 00:45:04.620
I don’t know if they really respect
teachers here also.

00:45:04.620 --> 00:45:19.860
This has come out of a philosophy:
"Let the children express themselves

00:45:19.860 --> 00:45:27.210
and let them be free!"
Which is wrong, for why are there parents?

00:45:27.720 --> 00:45:29.940
I always said,
"They should hang from the trees!"

00:45:29.940 --> 00:45:33.570
What is the use of parents
if parents can’t do anything about it?

00:45:41.440 --> 00:45:43.780
Some were saying,
"Mother, we were also like that."

00:45:43.780 --> 00:45:48.970
I said, "This generation is much worse.
Even if you were like that, so what?"

00:45:48.970 --> 00:45:52.900
They said, "We changed with Sahaja Yoga."
I said, "How to run the school now?

00:45:52.900 --> 00:46:02.440
We have to run the school at this age!"
No self-respect, no respect for anything!

00:46:02.440 --> 00:46:07.300
At least seventy percent
of the children are like that.

00:46:07.300 --> 00:46:12.640
Even the girls are terrible.
They don’t brush their teeth,

00:46:13.180 --> 00:46:16.900
they don’t want to take a bath,
they’ll cry for anything, make such a fuss.

00:46:32.160 --> 00:46:39.990
I had a talk this time with them,
brought lots of presents for them.

00:46:39.990 --> 00:46:43.680
They were nice to me
and they were listening to me.

00:46:43.680 --> 00:46:46.350
But Grégoire said,
"They are hypocritical, Mother!"

00:46:48.810 --> 00:46:53.940
He went and warned them:
"If you behave like this,

00:46:53.940 --> 00:46:59.370
we’ll not have you back in the house!"
So they said, "Where will you send us then?"

00:46:59.370 --> 00:47:01.680
He said, "We’ll send you
to a lunatic asylum!"

00:47:06.660 --> 00:47:09.840
The new generation that is coming
is going to be much worse than you,

00:47:09.840 --> 00:47:22.020
I tell you, in the West. Be careful!
All these theories come up,

00:47:22.020 --> 00:47:25.560
but without experimenting,
they just employ them.

00:47:25.560 --> 00:47:36.750
It’s very dangerous to do all this.
First experiment and see how it works!

00:47:45.680 --> 00:47:50.840
On the other hand,
they want to criticise our school,

00:47:50.840 --> 00:47:58.670
compared to horrible schools in France!
This boy Johannes was sent to a French school

00:47:58.670 --> 00:48:02.240
and he wrote to me,
"I can’t go to that school.

00:48:02.240 --> 00:48:10.160
The boys are doing dirty things
all the time. I can’t bear it."

00:48:17.680 --> 00:48:21.820
Children below twelve years
are taking to drugs, smoking.

00:48:24.820 --> 00:48:45.976
It is such a spoilt atmosphere.

00:48:45.976 --> 00:48:46.024
We see it in society
in another very strange way,

00:48:46.024 --> 00:48:46.095
where prisoners in jail –
they’re more concerned about their welfare

00:48:46.095 --> 00:48:46.136
than the people they have done damage to.

00:48:46.136 --> 00:48:46.152
Prisoners where?

00:48:46.152 --> 00:48:46.212
When they’re in jail,
lots of people in society are saying,

00:48:46.212 --> 00:48:46.275
"Oh, we must look after them.
We must do this, we must do that."

00:48:46.275 --> 00:48:46.840
But the people they have robbed
or killed or maimed – nothing.

00:48:46.840 --> 00:49:06.190
It’s a Vatican idea,
to support all war criminals – "compassion".

00:49:06.190 --> 00:49:14.290
The worst is France, you know.
Once we had to go by bus from the station,

00:49:16.831 --> 00:49:24.640
got into a bus, myself and Marie.
First, one gentleman walked in:

00:49:24.640 --> 00:49:30.070
he was absolutely mad,
and he sat in his chair

00:49:30.070 --> 00:49:34.390
and started saying things.
I said, "What is he talking about?"

00:49:35.320 --> 00:49:39.220
She said, "He’s decrying the war,
what has gone wrong in the war."

00:49:39.220 --> 00:49:42.910
"So loudly?" I said, "He’s a bhoot.
Everybody will catch bhoots from him!"

00:49:44.110 --> 00:49:50.590
She said, "Mother, it’s all right."
Then another lady walked in, same style.

00:49:50.590 --> 00:49:54.130
Then another gentleman.
There were four or five by the time we arrived.

00:49:55.660 --> 00:50:00.220
And they were otherwise normal.
They would take their tickets, pay for that,

00:50:00.220 --> 00:50:04.090
otherwise all right.
But all the time talking like this.

00:50:04.090 --> 00:50:07.630
I said, "They should be arrested
and put in some lunatic asylum!"

00:50:08.740 --> 00:50:12.340
Marie said,
"The French are very compassionate."

00:50:12.340 --> 00:50:21.010
I said, "Compassionate to whom?"
Absolutely mad. Absolutely.

00:50:21.010 --> 00:50:27.580
I said, "They can hit anyone."
She said, "After all, they are mad."

00:50:27.580 --> 00:50:36.400
"Why do you want to mix them up with others?"
They said, "There are so many now.

00:50:37.000 --> 00:50:42.520
By living with society, they’ll improve."
It never happens.

00:50:44.170 --> 00:50:47.770
In India we don’t have so many mad people.
We don’t have schizophrenia at all.

00:50:50.590 --> 00:50:53.650
Either they are mad or they are sane,
there’s nothing in-between.

00:50:55.240 --> 00:51:02.290
With schizophrenia, they live like normal
and suddenly they become mad.

00:51:02.290 --> 00:51:07.390
Like an attack comes to them.
That we don’t have.

00:51:09.880 --> 00:51:26.230
It must be drinking, must be perversions,
or suppressions.

00:51:34.550 --> 00:51:39.110
It’s predicted that sixty-five percent
of Americans will become schizophrenic!

00:51:40.070 --> 00:51:51.830
You dare not go there!
I don’t know from where it comes.

00:51:51.830 --> 00:51:59.270
Is religious fanaticism
the same thing as madness?

00:51:59.270 --> 00:52:13.340
I think it must be that.
Confessions and this religious fundamentalism.

00:52:13.340 --> 00:52:18.920
I think Christians are the worst,
because at least Muslims,

00:52:18.920 --> 00:52:22.670
you know they are fundamentalist.
And Jews, you know.

00:52:22.670 --> 00:52:32.600
But Christians are sophisticated
fundamentalists. And that’s what happens.

00:52:32.600 --> 00:52:40.460
This Vatican is already on its way out;
I think so, absolutely.

00:52:43.670 --> 00:52:49.130
There’s a book written,
"In the Name of God" – horrible.

00:52:49.130 --> 00:52:52.460
Have you read that book?
It’s banned in India.

00:52:52.460 --> 00:52:53.990
No, it’s available here, Mother.

00:52:53.990 --> 00:53:01.446
It’s here? This gentleman came
to Sahaja Yoga after writing that book.

00:53:01.446 --> 00:53:10.100
He’s a very nice Englishman.
It says that Pope John Paul I

00:53:10.100 --> 00:53:20.630
was murdered by this Pope.
And nine million dollars were counterfeited

00:53:20.630 --> 00:53:26.630
and distributed through the Vatican.
What sort of organisation is it?

00:53:28.760 --> 00:53:33.650
After that, thirteen people were murdered
just to hide the secret.

00:53:35.180 --> 00:53:45.650
Now, every week in Italy,
there is some exposure of this Vatican.

00:53:45.650 --> 00:53:53.990
Roberto Calvi was murdered:
they said he hanged himself on a bridge.

00:53:55.430 --> 00:54:01.310
Calvi was murdered because he knew
the secret about the death of this Pope.

00:54:02.450 --> 00:54:11.000
The man who murdered him is a Mafia man,
and he has confessed:

00:54:13.160 --> 00:54:21.290
"The Vatican asked for my services,
and they paid for this murder."

00:54:21.290 --> 00:54:24.950
Then they asked Mr Hurd about this:
"Why didn't you do something

00:54:27.170 --> 00:54:32.030
when this fellow was hanged here?"
He said, "Because we don't want our judges

00:54:32.030 --> 00:54:38.780
to be murdered, our lawyers to be murdered."
Judges were murdered in Italy!

00:54:38.780 --> 00:54:42.320
What a dangerous place it is.
So I am there now.

00:54:53.320 --> 00:55:00.100
Also this Anglican Church,
absolute nonsense.

00:55:00.100 --> 00:55:04.810
And they know they are not truthful,
that’s why they are after us.

00:55:06.220 --> 00:55:14.530
They’re aware of it. Such falsehood!
In all religions it has happened like that,

00:55:15.040 --> 00:55:21.970
but maximum in the Christian religion.
Because it’s so sophisticated outward,

00:55:21.970 --> 00:55:27.640
inside what’s happening you don’t know –
like an amoebic cyst growing inside,

00:55:27.640 --> 00:55:38.650
coming out in thousands. Such hypocrisy!
And the people who believe in them

00:55:38.650 --> 00:55:45.820
are innocent, very good people.
And they are misled.

00:55:51.870 --> 00:55:56.310
That may be the reason
I was born in a Christian family:

00:55:56.310 --> 00:56:14.580
to find out all the nonsense.
They have no idea what these priests are up to.

00:56:14.580 --> 00:56:22.170
Also this lady who got the Peace Prize,
Mother Teresa:

00:56:22.170 --> 00:56:26.670
such a hot-tempered woman, I tell you.
I don’t know how you can give her a prize!

00:56:26.670 --> 00:56:36.570
She collected money from the Bengalis
and got hold of some barracks.

00:56:36.570 --> 00:56:41.340
Brings people who are dying,
puts them there, converts them.

00:56:43.380 --> 00:56:49.680
She cannot cure anybody,
gives no relief, no medicines, nothing –

00:56:49.680 --> 00:56:51.750
just to convert.
And she gets a Peace Prize!

00:56:51.750 --> 00:57:02.280
I met her once going to Calcutta.
She came on the plane,

00:57:04.710 --> 00:57:11.756
and she said, "I want to sit in front."
They said, "No, this is for sick people,

00:57:11.756 --> 00:57:18.360
you can’t sit here."
"No, I want to sit here only!"

00:57:26.430 --> 00:57:29.850
She was jumping from here to there –
she’s very thin, you know.

00:57:32.580 --> 00:57:37.140
For half an hour she was jumping with temper.
I said, "What is this?"

00:57:37.140 --> 00:57:42.000
"No, I am Mother Teresa!"
Then they literally put her down

00:57:42.000 --> 00:57:48.870
when the plane started.
And this lady should get the Prize for Peace!

00:57:52.230 --> 00:57:58.320
Even in Ethiopia,
she’s just converting people when dying.

00:57:58.320 --> 00:58:03.450
Because once you convert,
you will go to God immediately!

00:58:03.450 --> 00:58:17.250
Only you have to have the brand!
This ordination and ordination.

00:58:17.250 --> 00:58:19.061
What do you call it?
Ordation or ordination?

00:58:19.061 --> 00:58:19.080
Ordination, Mother.

00:58:19.080 --> 00:58:24.810
Ordination.
Women are stupid to fight for it.

00:58:24.810 --> 00:58:39.570
They must have a platform to speak,
the ladies must think: "Why only the men?"

00:58:39.570 --> 00:58:50.760
Hindus are equally misled by nonsense,
but the only advantage in Hindu religion

00:58:50.760 --> 00:59:00.210
is that it’s not organised:
there’s no Pope or Archbishop of Canterbury.

00:59:06.530 --> 00:59:22.460
The way they mix up politics with religion!
The Christian Democratic Party

00:59:22.460 --> 00:59:31.520
has ruled Italy for forty years.
There are seven other parties,

00:59:34.460 --> 00:59:54.470
fighting with each other.
It’s a funny type of government,

00:59:54.470 --> 00:59:59.300
in the doldrums all the time,
with thirty-two percent of votes.

00:59:59.300 --> 01:00:19.070
And French are Catholics of the worst type.
There's one advantage in Catholicism:

01:00:19.070 --> 01:00:28.070
you can drink as much as you like,
and for the French, their spiritual food

01:00:28.070 --> 01:00:30.560
is just drinking.

01:00:38.100 --> 01:00:44.940
Antonio went to see the judge
about this case. A nice judge:

01:00:44.940 --> 01:00:48.510
for that little boy
he gave a verdict of nine pages.

01:00:49.770 --> 01:00:54.960
He mentioned me as respectable
and Sahaja Yogis as very good people.

01:00:54.960 --> 01:01:02.820
And when Antonio went to see him,
the judge offered him wine.

01:01:03.600 --> 01:01:07.410
He said, "We don’t drink."
He was surprised that a Frenchman doesn't.

01:01:12.600 --> 01:01:17.910
In Australia, now they think
drinking is bad, isn’t it?

01:01:17.910 --> 01:01:26.382
There’s a new trend coming up,
respecting people who do not drink.

01:01:26.382 --> 01:01:26.438
The breweries are spending
a lot more money to advertise,

01:01:26.438 --> 01:01:26.478
meaning people are not drinking so much.

01:01:26.478 --> 01:01:26.542
A doctor was telling me,
"I've seen more people who don't drink."

01:01:26.542 --> 01:01:53.610
Really? Also it’s expensive,
with recession!

01:01:53.610 --> 01:01:56.880
Recession is a blessing in a way.

01:01:56.880 --> 01:02:07.830
The same thing is happening
with smoking to Australians. It’s lessening.

01:02:07.830 --> 01:02:09.199
Smoking also?

01:02:09.199 --> 01:02:09.210
I think so.

01:02:09.210 --> 01:02:15.240
That’s the real blessing.
Vishuddhi would be all right

01:02:15.240 --> 01:02:20.820
if smoking goes out.
Too much money has ruined them,

01:02:20.820 --> 01:02:22.620
so it’s better to have some recession.

01:02:22.620 --> 01:02:26.820
By the way,
I was thinking about the house for you.

01:02:29.280 --> 01:02:35.940
I found that houses in farmlands
are much cheaper.

01:02:36.510 --> 01:02:40.710
You should get a big house
which is dilapidated,

01:02:40.710 --> 01:02:43.740
instead of buying this one,
because it’s on the street.

01:02:43.740 --> 01:02:46.200
If you start singing tomorrow,
you’ll get police.

01:02:47.870 --> 01:02:59.000
Best is to find a place a little far away,
some sort of farmland,

01:02:59.000 --> 01:03:08.300
so we could pitch tents there,
and so they will not disturb you.

01:03:09.380 --> 01:03:17.360
Somebody suggested
they should buy this house.

01:03:19.430 --> 01:03:20.457
That was Brisbane.

01:03:20.458 --> 01:03:29.691
In Brisbane, not here?
This is all right, but for Sahaja Yoga

01:03:29.690 --> 01:03:46.300
you have to go a little outside.
Just find out. You might get it.

01:03:46.300 --> 01:03:48.550
They have a very small house in Brisbane.&nbsp;

01:03:59.460 --> 01:04:03.030
It may be convenient for working people,

01:04:03.030 --> 01:04:10.470
but for meditation, I think you have to be
a little away from the city.

01:04:12.780 --> 01:04:21.210
In Sahaja Yoga we see to all conveniences:
like the puja should be on a Sunday.

01:04:27.420 --> 01:04:37.200
Formerly you had to go to the Himalayas
at least, for your ascent.

01:04:37.200 --> 01:04:48.990
So it’s very convenient and comfortable.
Still, a house should be a little away

01:04:48.990 --> 01:04:57.930
from the madding crowd.
After all, you have cars,

01:04:57.930 --> 01:05:00.750
so what does it matter?
Five miles here or five miles there.

01:05:00.750 --> 01:05:06.900
The best thing is to go for such a house.
And if it is dilapidated, it’s better,

01:05:06.900 --> 01:05:11.820
because you can renovate it yourself
and enjoy that renovation.

01:05:11.820 --> 01:05:33.549
Why are you crying? For daddy?
Oh my God! The security of daddy!

01:05:44.060 --> 01:05:52.100
For Sarah, I wanted to tell you something:
I didn’t know that she plays cello.

01:05:55.880 --> 01:05:59.750
Her husband comes from
an aristocratic family,

01:06:01.100 --> 01:06:03.620
has lots of lands and things,
and business in transports;

01:06:03.620 --> 01:06:09.380
he’s doing very well.
For him to come here would be like a beggar.

01:06:10.760 --> 01:06:17.360
He can come just to visit.
She can learn Indian music there.

01:06:17.360 --> 01:06:24.590
If she has done cello, she can do very well,
because it’s the same style as sitar.

01:06:25.250 --> 01:06:35.690
She might be able to do it easily.
They should have written it down,

01:06:35.690 --> 01:06:41.392
that she is a cello player:
then Austria is the best place.

01:06:41.392 --> 01:07:01.140
It was on the marriage form,
but it was abbreviated.

01:07:01.140 --> 01:07:15.090
Are you sure?
There were five hundred marriage forms.

01:07:15.090 --> 01:07:22.230
It doesn’t matter, it’s for the good,
because cello is over now.

01:07:22.230 --> 01:07:26.700
If she becomes a good sitar player,
she’ll be known all over the world.

01:07:29.880 --> 01:07:36.450
Western music you play in a group;
you don’t have that much creativity,

01:07:37.560 --> 01:07:44.400
it’s all written down.
Indian music is not like that.

01:07:49.410 --> 01:08:01.020
Individually you can be of great renown.
So she has a good chance.

01:08:02.370 --> 01:08:08.220
I think she can learn violin there.
Indian violin is very good.

01:08:08.220 --> 01:08:17.250
Or she could learn sitar, sarod, anything.
Once you know a string instrument,

01:08:17.250 --> 01:08:28.140
you can do that better.
And it’s not teamwork:

01:08:28.140 --> 01:08:33.930
you play alone, single.
That’s something great.

01:08:33.930 --> 01:08:38.610
And they’ll appreciate it
coming from a Western girl.

01:08:40.110 --> 01:08:42.720
Even our government
gives a scholarship for that.

01:08:53.660 --> 01:08:57.106
Beeath is the one who got it.

01:08:57.106 --> 01:09:01.670
And Simon from England.

01:09:01.669 --> 01:09:13.459
Simon is from Italy,
married in England. He got a scholarship.

01:09:17.540 --> 01:09:20.720
One has to be a good Sahaja Yogi,
otherwise the one who gets you this

01:09:22.100 --> 01:09:24.890
is Debu Chaudhuri.
And he wouldn’t give it to somebody

01:09:24.890 --> 01:09:31.850
who is not a good Sahaja Yogi.
He asked me, "Mother, what do you think

01:09:31.850 --> 01:09:33.200
about the Sahaja Yoga part?"

01:09:35.090 --> 01:09:39.440
Debu Chaudhuri had this problem
of the "artist’s thumb".

01:09:39.439 --> 01:09:48.679
He couldn’t play for so many years
because he used to get cramps

01:09:48.680 --> 01:09:55.130
on his thumbs. So I cured him.
He got completely all right,

01:09:55.129 --> 01:10:00.949
and then he started playing again.
Then he became Dean of Faculty of Arts,

01:10:03.229 --> 01:10:14.089
and started performances all over.
He made some ragas for me.

01:10:14.090 --> 01:10:19.100
Now he has got a very high title,
Padma Bhushan.

01:10:25.700 --> 01:10:33.770
He is very much indebted to Sahaja Yoga.
He thinks Sahaja Yoga gave him steadiness

01:10:33.770 --> 01:11:55.130
and these blessings,
and that’s how he has achieved it.

01:12:21.250 --> 01:12:24.460
In Sahaja Yoga one should not worry:
everything works out.

01:12:24.460 --> 01:12:30.160
Whatever is an obstruction
really is for our progress.

01:12:30.160 --> 01:12:36.370
This case in France has helped us so much.
Everything is for our progress.

01:12:36.370 --> 01:12:41.080
If there’s an obstruction,
it is for us to jump out of it.

01:12:43.810 --> 01:12:51.610
So one should never worry about anything.
It’s all worked out.

01:12:51.610 --> 01:13:00.820
This time there was a miracle
when you came to India:

01:13:00.820 --> 01:13:07.240
we had all these silver things
and presents put in a truck.

01:13:08.260 --> 01:13:13.390
They told me, "We have filled the truck
and we are going to leave."

01:13:13.390 --> 01:13:17.710
I said, "No, tonight you are not to leave.
Go tomorrow morning."

01:13:17.710 --> 01:13:20.440
They couldn’t understand.
I said, "No, nothing doing."

01:13:20.440 --> 01:13:25.780
And that night, all the trucks
were plundered on the way by dacoits.

01:13:25.780 --> 01:13:36.760
So next morning they started.
And they came close to Ganapatipule,

01:13:36.760 --> 01:13:40.390
to Jakadevi. Most of the time,
there are accidents there.

01:13:40.390 --> 01:13:45.010
Must be some sort of a bhoot there.
This truck lost control,

01:13:45.580 --> 01:13:50.074
the wheel started coming out – big problem.
It was on a slope,

01:13:50.074 --> 01:13:54.790
so it started moving backwards.
The boys jumped out, and the driver,

01:13:55.390 --> 01:13:58.360
thinking, "Now what will happen?"
with all the things inside there.

01:13:58.360 --> 01:14:01.630
It started moving,
suddenly turned at right angles,

01:14:01.630 --> 01:14:11.500
and then again at right angles,
and stopped near a stone platform.

01:14:11.500 --> 01:14:15.670
It just stopped there.
They thought it was finished:

01:14:15.670 --> 01:14:20.230
"Where is it going, moving by itself?"
Then a bus came that side.

01:14:20.230 --> 01:14:23.200
If this had not happened,
the bus would have collided.

01:14:23.200 --> 01:14:29.830
I have seen it myself being stopped.
No one can believe how it happened.

01:14:31.390 --> 01:14:39.310
They used the platform for taking out things.
People went and got another truck.

01:14:39.310 --> 01:14:45.910
And nothing was destroyed, nothing.
Not a single bit.

01:14:45.910 --> 01:14:51.580
So, that’s what it is.
Sahaja Yoga is something

01:14:51.580 --> 01:14:54.190
one has to experience
and then believe in it.

01:14:54.190 --> 01:14:55.720
Everything works out.

01:15:09.740 --> 01:15:11.202
So now I’ll take your leave.

01:15:11.202 --> 01:15:11.870
May God bless you!

